    title: "A Sensitization Workshop for the Federal Ministry of Health and Social Welfare on Understanding Intersex and Inclusive Intersex Healthcare",
    text: "Intersex Nigeria hosted a workshop in Abuja with officials from the Federal Ministry of Health and Social Welfare, focusing on the need to include intersex individuals in healthcare planning and design. This engagement aimed to address barriers faced by intersex persons, such as unrecorded births, stigma in healthcare settings, and exclusion from essential healthcare services. \n\nThe workshop brought together 34 representatives from various departments within the Ministry, creating discussions aimed at raising awareness and promoting inclusive healthcare policies. Participants explored strategic collaborations to enhance the well-being of intersex individuals and provide affirming healthcare services. \n\nA key objective was to bridge knowledge gaps and advocate for reforms that prioritize intersex rights. The officials called for the development of a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) to guide the protection and promotion of intersex health, along with specific healthcare policies or modifying existing ones that uphold their rights and dignity.\n\nDuring the sessions, stakeholders emphasized the importance of evidence-based policy-making, urging collaboration with other institutions to address systemic issues in intersex healthcare. The need for a Social and Behavioral Change Communication (SBCC) plan was discussed, targeting media, policymakers, and the public to build understanding and acceptance of intersex issues.\n\nAction points emerged from the workshop, including the integration of intersex perspectives into existing health policies. The workshop marked a significant step towards ensuring equitable healthcare access for intersex individuals in Nigeria.",
    description: "Intersex Nigeria hosted a workshop in Abuja with officials from the Federal Ministry of Health and Social Welfare, focusing on the need to include intersex individuals in healthcare planning and design.",
