    title: "National Youth Service Sensitization (Youth Focused Advocacy) 2024",
    text: "In May 2024, Intersex Nigeria continued its step forward in its mission to promote awareness and visibility by visiting the National Youth Service Corps (NYSC) orientation camp in Kubwa, FCT Abuja. This initiative program aimed to educate young individuals about the understanding of sex characteristics and gender, as well as the lived realities of intersex persons in Nigeria.\n\nIntersex Nigeria's team engaged several individuals in discussions that highlighted the need for visibility and understanding of intersex. By addressing prevalent myths and misconceptions surrounding intersex individuals in Nigeria.\n\nDuring the visit, the team talked about the unique challenges and needs faced by intersex persons. They underscored the importance of preventing discrimination and promoting inclusion at all levels of society. This program not only aimed to educate the youth but also to cultivate empathy and support for intersex rights. A crucial topic of discussion was the alarming issue of Intersex Genital Mutilation (IGM). Intersex Nigeria is committed to advocating for the end of this harmful practice, which has long-term physical and psychological consequences.\n\nThe visit to the NYSC camp built a sense of empathy and solidarity among the reached youths and a community for intersex individuals.",
    description: "In May 2024, Intersex Nigeria continued its step forward in its mission to promote awareness and visibility by visiting the National Youth Service Corps (NYSC) orientation camp in Kubwa, FCT Abuja. This initiative program aimed to educate young individuals about the understanding of sex characteristics and gender, as well as the lived realities of intersex persons in Nigeria.",
